      "side": 1,
      "message": "[info] Line 1315: Minor leak on the extension-handled path: when `iOSConnectedCb_(...)` returns true the code `return`s before `finalizeIOSCallRequest()`, so the id is intentionally left in `transientIOSCallRequests_` for in-process dedup — but it is never erased. For an ephemeral notification extension this is fine, yet every extension-handled call permanently consumes one of the 1024 slots, so a long-lived process would eventually saturate the bound and start dropping new calls (see comment on the size check). Also note `if (!shared) return;` at the top of this cert callback leaks the reservation on shutdown. Neither is blocking; a brief comment documenting the deliberate \u0027keep reserved\u0027 semantics would help future readers.",
      "revId": "6ee1e9578da3c4a7d676e764673feea011746d3b",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
