      "writtenOn": "2026-07-12T18:32:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 1901: New tradeoff introduced by switching from eviction (PS3) to backpressure (PS4): because `reserveIOSCallRequest()` is called *before* certificate verification, an untrusted peer can flood the extension with up to 1024 distinct call-request ids (connType videoCall/audioCall). Each reservation is only released when the async `findCertificate()` completes and `foundPeerDevice()` fails via `releaseIOSCallRequest()`. If an attacker announces new ids faster than the cert lookups resolve, `transientIOSCallRequests_` stays saturated and `reserveIOSCallRequest()` returns false for *legitimate* call requests, so `return true` silently drops them and the call never rings — a pre-auth DoS on incoming calls. Consider deferring the reservation until after `foundPeerDevice()` succeeds (reserve inside the cert callback for authenticated peers only), or tracking untrusted reservations under a separate, smaller budget so unauthenticated floods cannot starve verified peers.",
      "revId": "6ee1e9578da3c4a7d676e764673feea011746d3b",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    }
